// tunnel, registry and folder picker run for real against it. A clone address containing "fail" is refused as clone_failed; one containing "private" is, unless the request carries a credential.
// For a continue onto this machine it also answers the handshake (host.hello), git.inspect (FAKE_HOST_REPO: the repository every folder
// holds, as JSON; unset: not a repository), chat.prepareContinue (a folder that does not exist under FAKE_HOST_ROOT is refused as
// directory_missing), chat.subscribe, chat.release, git.carryApply and git.carryDrop; every call it answers is appended to
// FAKE_HOST_LOG (one JSON line: method and params) so a spec can read what the app asked.
// With FAKE_HOST_CHATS_SOCK set, the chat methods (chat.start, chat.send, chat.stop, chat.answer, chat.permit, chat.subscribe) are bridged to the resident fake Host
// in host-chats.cjs, which keeps chats and turns running while this tunnel comes and goes. While the file FAKE_HOST_OFFLINE exists this `ssh` is down: it
// exits at once, and one already up checks before every I/O boundary as well as periodically while idle. FAKE_HOST_HARNESSES (JSON) is what `status` reports,
// with FAKE_HOST_LOCAL_NETWORK as its `localNetwork`. The machine named by FAKE_HOST_ASLEEP restarted and waits at the login window: its tunnel never comes
